<Base title="About" description="Ryadh Dahimene: product at ClickHouse, previously Elastic, a PhD at CNAM, and two early startups.">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    <strong>ClickHouse (2022–).</strong> I joined as a consulting architect, then moved into product management: first
    integrations, where I worked on <a href="/writing/clickpipes-is-generally-available/">ClickPipes</a>, and now AI/ML.
    Along the way I worked on the acquisitions of PeerDB, HyperDX, LibreChat and Langfuse.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Elastic (2017–2021).</strong> Consulting architect in the professional services team, then manager of the
    UK, Middle East and Africa services team, helping customers run search and analytics at scale on the Elastic
    Stack.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Consulting (2015–2017).</strong> Big data and data insights manager at Ysance in Paris, where I designed the
    “<a href="/writing/cdv/" lang="fr">chaîne de valeur data</a>” methodology and ran the Paris Data Meetup.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>PhD (CNAM, Paris).</strong> A PhD in computer science at the Conservatoire National des Arts et Métiers,
    on filtering and recommendation in social networks, followed by two years as a lecturer and research assistant.
    See <a href="/papers/">papers</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Early ventures.</strong> I founded <strong>Think IT</strong>, a software consultancy in Algiers
    (2009–2014), and co-founded <strong>Jib.li</strong> in Paris (2011–2014), a seed-funded crowdshipping platform
    where travellers carry parcels for other people (<a href="/writing/jibli/">press story</a>).
  </p>

  <p>
    I live in Barcelona. The best way to reach me is by <a href="mailto:dahimene.ryadh@gmail.com">email</a>.
  </p>
